## Questions with defaults (Tuesday answers at the stamp; every default is already assumed above)
- **Q1 (D1; STOP-CLASS: S4 answers it in words).** Default: the guard refuses (`StorageFailed`, nothing removed) only a record whose payload names an ACTIVE key of the verified ring while the probe under the current key fails; records under a foreign, unknown or revoked key are removed as today, so U04 and U13 stand unchanged. Alternative: the second reader's sketch read literally (refuse every record whose key id is not an active key of the ring): MEASURED as the mutant `mLiteralSketch`, it turns U04 (row r2) and U13 red, so it needs two landed cells' assertions changed and makes abandoned and foreign records removable only by an operator. Cost of the default: none of the landed behaviour changes; the residual of S8 stays a named limit.
- Q2 (D5). Default: N3 and N5 IN (each a few lines, each red first on macOS), N2 OUT (needs a decision on a written key and a fault after the write). Alternative: N3 and N5 out too (drop R18, R19 and their hunks; the guard and N7 alone).
- Q3 (D3, D4). Default: `StorageFailed` for a linked partition folder and for a record folder swapped for a link. Alternative: `KeyNotAvailable` for the partition folder (it holds the key folder too).
- Q4 (U22's shape). Default: the red-first fault is the store's own data protection services released under it (`((IDisposable)store.ProtectionServices).Dispose()`, the existing `internal` member the tests already see), a failure of the protection that is not the record's. Alternative: an internal test seam in the product (more product code) or no cell (the guard unproven).
